
This directory holds the runtime library modules for the native
code implementation of BCPL for Raspberry Pi machines using the ARMv8
architecture. It uses 64-bit registers and execute essentially the the
modern ARM machine code used by Raspberry Pi Models 3, 4 and 5.

These libraries and the codegenerator (now called com/bcplcgarmv8.b)
and are based on those for the ARMv7.  What is planned is both a cross
compiler running on the Cintcode BCPL system and a native code version
running directly on an ARMv8 Raspberry Pi such as the Model 5.

This is still in the very early stages of under development. Initially
this system will be limited to 32-bit BCPL but will eventually provide
native code compilers for both 32 and 64 bit BCPL that will run on
modern varsions of the Raspberry Pi. The armv8 compiler is in
BCPL/cintcode/combcplarmv8.b and BCPL/cintcode/com/bcpcgarmv8.b

This directory is called BCPL/cintcode/armv8. The version for earlier
Raspberry PIs running ARMv7, such as Model 2, is in directory
BCPL/cintcode/armv7.

